  "subject": "history-social-studies",
  "summary": "A semester of Grade 7 world history, from the first cities to the eve of the 1500s: ancient Mesopotamia, the Silk Roads, the Islamic world, the empires of West Africa, medieval Europe, and the Maya, Aztec and Inca. Students read primary sources as historians do, asking who made them, when, why and for whom, and write evidence-based explanations and arguments. Six units, each with a student overview, a teacher guide with a five-day plan, a lesson, assignments, an assessment with a rubric and an answer key.",
  "title": "World History 7",
